1
00:00:00,261 --> 00:00:04,584
When the dropdown says Claude, you might
ask who makes the model, where it runs,

2
00:00:04,795 --> 00:00:06,074
and which tool you're using.

3
00:00:06,518 --> 00:00:09,773
Those are three questions. The maker
publishes the model,

4
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:14,550
a provider or platform offers access,
and the client gives you a workflow.

5
00:00:14,883 --> 00:00:17,828
In this lesson, the catalogs are a dated
snapshot.

6
00:00:18,206 --> 00:00:21,403
Your approved picker tells you what is
available for work.

7
00:00:22,994 --> 00:00:27,947
Open the OpenAI model catalog and
compare the entries for GPT six point

8
00:00:28,002 --> 00:00:29,326
two Sol and Astra.

9
00:00:29,805 --> 00:00:34,008
In the snapshot, Sol is positioned for
everyday coding and agent work.

10
00:00:34,476 --> 00:00:37,954
Astra is positioned for more demanding
reasoning and coding.

11
00:00:38,354 --> 00:00:41,196
Notice the input and output section on
each card.

12
00:00:41,652 --> 00:00:44,511
If you need transcription or image
generation,

13
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:48,316
read the relevant entry instead of
inferring it from the name.

14
00:00:49,702 --> 00:00:53,427
In Anthropic’s catalog, find Haiku,
Sonnet, Opus, and Fable.

15
00:00:53,766 --> 00:00:58,294
Their cards describe different speed,
workload, and capability tradeoffs.

16
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:02,145
The provider table matters when you use
Claude Code remotely.

17
00:01:02,456 --> 00:01:06,695
Two environments can show the same
family name while resolving a shortcut

18
00:01:06,695 --> 00:01:07,345
differently.

19
00:01:07,591 --> 00:01:12,295
Record the exact model ID or selector
label you can verify in the approved

20
00:01:12,295 --> 00:01:12,945
session.

21
00:01:14,325 --> 00:01:17,984
In Microsoft Foundry, inspect the
publisher on a model card.

22
00:01:18,368 --> 00:01:23,158
The catalog includes models published by
Microsoft as well as models from other

23
00:01:23,158 --> 00:01:23,808
providers.

24
00:01:24,189 --> 00:01:29,533
You may see Microsoft’s MAI or Phi
families. MAI Code two Flash was a

25
00:01:29,533 --> 00:01:31,697
